# Normalise line endings so contributors on Windows, macOS and Linux
# don't produce whole-file diffs. Lenses are read by agents, so a stray
# CRLF flipping every line is pure review noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# JAR manifest main sections end with a blank line by format.
integrations/burp-montoya/MANIFEST.MF whitespace=-blank-at-eof
scripts/ghidra/GhidraBundleLocationAgent.mf whitespace=-blank-at-eof

# Fixtures are read as source code by the audit pipeline. Keep them LF
# regardless of platform so a proof recipe's line numbers stay stable.
fixtures/** text eol=lf

# The fixture corpus is deliberately defective code. It is written from scratch,
# it is not runnable, and it is never imported by anything that ships — its only
# consumer is the evaluation in fixtures/EXPECTED.md.
#
# `linguist-vendored` is what a repository can express here: it keeps the corpus
# out of language statistics and out of GitHub's rendered diffs and code-search
# results by default, which is the closest thing to "not analysed" that
# .gitattributes reaches. It does NOT suppress a code scanner — CodeQL, Semgrep,
# Snyk and Dependabot each read their own configuration, not this file. Anyone
# wiring one of those up must exclude `fixtures/**` there as well; see
# fixtures/README.md, which states this in the same words so the two do not drift.
fixtures/** linguist-vendored
